-- CA_0307_la_city_downey_el_segundo_2026.sql
-- LA-cities slice: the last two held cities, Downey and El Segundo (Nov 3 2026 General Municipal Election).
-- Neither City Clerk ever posted a qualified / certified candidate list (Downey: Notice of City Election only;
-- El Segundo: a nomination-papers pulled/returned log). SOURCE (approved by Chris Andrews 2026-10-13): the LA County
-- RR/CC Candidate Statements app for election 4348 (https://apps.lavote.gov/candidate-statements/, API
-- /statements-api/oc/read/election/4348/contest, read 2026-10-13): contests 10443 (Downey D2), 10444 (Downey D4),
-- 10452 (El Segundo council). The app lists candidates who filed a ballot statement; El Segundo's three names match the
-- clerk's three returned nomination papers. Occupations below are the app's ballot designations.
--
-- EL SEGUNDO (at large, 5 members, council-chosen mayor; already modeled at large): 2 seats, 3 candidates.
--   Chris Pimentel (Mayor) and Ryan W. Baldino (Mayor Pro Tem) are the incumbents (both elected 2022); John Pickhaver.
--   Three filers for two seats, so no appointment in lieu (EC 10229) was possible.
--
-- DOWNEY (charter city, council-chosen rotating mayor). Resolution 24-8277 + the map adopted 2025-05-13 move Downey to
-- five discrete districts; under EC 21626(b) the new map first applies to District 2 and District 4 in Nov 2026
-- (D1, D3 and the citywide D5 seat follow in 2028). The DB had all five members on the whole-city polygon, so this:
--   * loads the NEW District 2 and District 4 polygons (X0001; LA RR/CC precinct layer Political_Boundaries/MapServer/34,
--     DST_CITY='DO', dissolved by DIV_CITY, read 2026-10-13; the layer already carries five discrete districts = the
--     2025 map; all five districts cover the TIGER place 0619766 at 0.9993, IoU 0.9988, seam-only overlaps);
--   * repoints the existing per-office 'District 2' / 'District 4' LOCAL rows onto them (each row holds one office:
--     Hector Sosa D2, Claudia M. Frometa D4), and retitles those two offices "Council Member (District N)"
--     (Frometa's "Mayor" title is the annual rotation, not a separate office).
--   D1 (Ortiz), D3 (Pemberton) and D5 (Trujillo, citywide until 2028) are not up and stay on the whole city.
--   Downey D2: Hector Sosa (incumbent), Maria Zaragoza.  Downey D4 (open; Frometa is term-limited): Martha Camacho
--   Rodriguez, Lissette Rivera, Carrie Uva.
--
-- RACES go on '2026 LA County General' (d91a20ce-557e-4615-a31b-5b2b3df2ed14); primary_party NULL; no party stored.
-- IDEMPOTENT: polygons NOT EXISTS-guarded; repoints/retitles are plain assignments; every insert NOT EXISTS-guarded.

BEGIN;

